# create-inside-try (#5): a try..finally whose FIRST protected statement is
# X := TFoo.Create. Fires on line 10 (Create inside the try); NOT on the correct
# pattern where the object is created before the try (line 15) and the try's first
# statement is SL.Add (line 16/17).
create-inside-try 10
!create-inside-try 15
!create-inside-try 16
!create-inside-try 17
